          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "default-page-number-assignment",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Default page number assignment"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The print dialog doesn’t understand the page numbers that are displayed in the running content. The print dialog only considers physical pages. Therefore, to print a range of pages as they are labeled in the document, you need to add the number of front matter pages (i.e., the non-numbered pages) to the page number range in the print dialog."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "For example, if you only want to print the first 5 pages labeled with a page number (e.g., 1-5), and there are 2 pages before the page labeled as page 1, you need to add 2 to both numbers in the range, giving you a physical page range of 3-7. That’s the range you need to enter into the print dialog."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "printing-page-ranges",
        "level": 1,
